    "body": "Looking at the README from https://www.npmjs.com/package/typescript-language-server\r\n\r\ntypescript-language-server needs for typescript@6\r\ntsc needs typescript@7",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I think that's not required. ~~The instruction in readme sync with the typescript version it depends(if you check the version history e.g. 5.3.0, the version in the instruction is just 5.3.0)~~\r\nPeople can install whatever version of typescript lower than 7.0 to get `ts_ls` work.\r\nIt'd be better to have an warning or tip in the comment instead of using a fixed version number.",
